WAY AHEAD: OWNER STEPS, IN ORDER

1. KYC (B1)
   - Register as Individual or Unregistered Business.
   - PAN name must match the bank account name exactly.
   - Submit all three site URLs: ai-borne.in, ssbmax.ai, actionstation.in.
   - Set the display name to ai-borne.
   - Before submitting, open each site signed out and confirm the four legal
     pages (Privacy, Terms, Refund & Cancellation, Contact) load and are linked
     in the footer.

2. LIVE-MODE WEBHOOK (after KYC approval)
   - Test mode and live mode have separate webhook lists. Create the
     ActionStation live webhook at the same razorpayWebhook URL with ONLY:
       payment.captured, refund.processed
     (no subscription.* events; ActionStation sells one-time orders only).
   - Use a live webhook secret. Store it in Secret Manager as
     RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET, then redeploy the function so it picks it up.
   - Tell the SSBMax side its live webhook will also receive ActionStation
     events. That is safe because of the filter (step 4), but check it.

3. LIVE KEYS (B3), TOGETHER FOR BOTH APPS
   - Replace RAZORPAY_KEY_ID and RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET with live keys in Secret
     Manager for ActionStation AND SSBMax in the same sitting.
   - Redeploy createRazorpayOrder, razorpayWebhook and any function that reads
     the key. Do not leave one app on test keys and the other on live keys
     against the same account.

4. FIRST REAL PAYMENT AND REFUND DRILL (B5)
   - Make one small real ActionStation payment, then refund it from the
     dashboard within the 7-day window.
   - Expect: order created, payment.captured returns 200, user becomes Pro,
     refund.processed returns 200, user returns to Free.
   - This is also the first LIVE proof of the SSBMax filter. In SSBMax's logs
     look for: "belongs to another app on the shared account -- acknowledged".
     It must return 200 and must not touch any SSBMax user.
   - If SSBMax logs "Underpayment detected" or returns 400 for the
     ActionStation payment, stop and fix the filter before taking real money.

5. ONGOING
   - Keep all four legal pages linked on every site footer (review looks at
     every submitted URL).
   - Keep price visible in INR before checkout (already: Rs 2,999 per year).
   - Never process a webhook without verifying X-Razorpay-Signature.
   - Always return 200 for events an app does not own. A 4xx makes Razorpay
     retry and can disable the webhook.
   - GST and invoicing approach still to decide (B9).

KNOWN RISKS TO WATCH
- Shared account: any new product on this account must stamp notes.source on
  its orders and ignore other sources, or it will collide with the others.
- Order notes carry userId and planId in the same shape across apps. The source
  stamp is the only thing telling them apart. Legacy SSBMax payments have no
  source and are treated as SSBMax's own.
- Stale app after a deploy: HTML is now no-cache, but a browser that already
  holds an old service worker needs one reload or update prompt.
- Cross-site copy must use ssbmax.ai, never ssbmax.in.

